== what just landed ==

full orbital visualization pipeline is live end-to-end:
- nodes zenka derives @INDEXCUBE position from IP (theta/phi/psi/omega)
- nodes pushes p7ref to discover via route-send every 13s
- discover appends p7ref to mcast packets
- web zenka fetches orbital data every 13s via route-send (not send.local —
  web plugin context requires route-send for cross-zenka calls)
- orbital.json at space.v7.ax: self + known nodes populated, glow_shells/channel/graph
  from graphics-matrix zenka
- visualization renders at http://127.0.0.1/ with Host: space.v7.ax header
- POST /context wired: browser sends zoom+intent, stored in web.space.templates.context
- kimi reconnect approval flush deployed (kimi.connect flushes pending on reconnect)

key architectural lessons from this session:
- web plugin context: use route-send, not send.local (send.local = httpd↔web IPC only)
- discover/nodes context: use send.local for cube-routed calls (route-send needs parent_route)
- reply handlers don't work in non-plugin zenki (discover, nodes) — use push pattern instead
- multi-dot command names (a.b.c) don't route — always single-dot with subcommand in args
- p7 module no-arg call: <[module.name]> not <[module.name]>->() (->() is stripped)
- p7c not p7 (binary was renamed)
- ptd -c not perl -c for syntax checks

